    "verdict": "NEGATIVE for the additive split. The additive open/loop decomposition (²H-calibrated) UNDER-predicts badly for A>2 (³H −37%, ³He −30%, ⁴He −64%). The collective full determinant (all edges as loops) does much better on the even-even line (²H 0.42×, ⁴He 0.94×) but is NON-monotone and non-predictive overall (³H 0.74×, ³He 0.30× — the p↔n mirror asymmetry splits the A=3 pair). Two honest conclusions (scope-(a)): (i) many-body binding is COLLECTIVE (all cross terms), NOT a sum of per-bond open+loop contributions — the proved dichotomy governs the single-bond g-order (²H) only; (ii) the collective determinant is the better many-body direction but not yet a predictor — its ⁴He ~6% and its ³He mirror residual are the open GAP-A-4 magnitude legs. No tuning, no selection."
